      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The rhetoric commonly employed by these groups is often built upon pseudoscientific and deeply flawed interpretations of evolutionary biology and sociology. A central tenet is the concept of \"white/European identity\" being biologically or culturally threatened by demographic changes, a notion often framed as existential survival. They frequently employ narratives of victimization, arguing that their group is under external pressure leading to inevitable replacement or subjugation. These justifications rarely rely on empirical evidence but rather on conspiratorial worldviews designed to foster an in-group/out-group dichotomy.",
